Subject: [PATCH] arm64: ship OpenSSH (ssh, sshd, scp, sftp) at boot

arm64 has no HaikuPorts openssh either -- see 0015's note on icu74, but
worse here: there is no port for this architecture at all, bootstrap or
not (build/jam/repositories/HaikuPorts/arm64's RemotePackageRepository
baseurl has an empty real "current" index for arm64, confirmed by fetching
it directly).

packages/openssh-10.4p1-1-arm64.hpkg is cross-built the same way 0012's
curl/wget/tar/gzip are, against this tree's own cross-compiler, openssl3
and zlib, using HaikuPorts' own net-misc/openssh patchset for 10.4p1
(github.com/haikuports/haikuports) -- OpenSSH's own ./configure already
has native Haiku support; the patchset only fixes BFS having no hardlinks
(ssh-keygen.c, hostfile.c, mux.c use rename() under __HAIKU__), two
gcc2-only scoping bugs harmless to keep, and points ~/.ssh at Haiku's
~/config/settings/ssh convention. Built without libedit, which is not in
the arm64 package set and only gives sftp's interactive prompt line
editing -- ssh/sshd/scp don't need it.

The package ships no settings/ssh of its own (packagefs mounts a package
read-only, and settings has to be writable) -- just data/openssh/*.default
templates and an empty data/openssh/empty for the privsep chroot. It
declares a package user/group (sshd, native .PackageInfo "users"/"groups"
blocks, not a HaikuPorts-only concept) for privilege separation.

data/system/boot/SshdKeygen materializes settings/ssh from those templates
and runs `ssh-keygen -A` for host keys on first boot. data/launch/sshd
runs it, then execs sshd -D, as one `/bin/sh -c "...; exec ..."` command on
a single service -- not SshdKeygen as its own `job` with the service
`requires`-ing it, which is the more obvious shape and was tried first.
`requires` only orders launch_daemon's own trigger, not completion: on a
freshly booted guest, where host-key generation can take several minutes
(ssh-keygen -A waiting on an EFI/QEMU guest's thin early-boot entropy
pool -- confirmed by comparing file timestamps: sshd_config at one point,
every ssh_host_*_key file ten minutes later), sshd was already running
with the `requires` form, had loaded zero host keys because none existed
yet when it started, and stayed that way forever -- offering an empty
host key algorithm list, which every client rejects with "no matching
host key type found" and which nothing afterward makes it reload. Chaining
onto one `;` makes the second command wait on the first no matter how long
that actually takes, which `requires` turned out not to guarantee.

The service launches sshd through `/bin/sh -c "... ; exec sshd -D"`, not
`launch /system/sbin/sshd -D` directly -- settled by hitting a second,
separate failure, not preference. Direct launch starts a process
launch_daemon is happy to report as running, with host keys loaded and
"Server listening on 0.0.0.0 port 22" in sshd's own debug log, and yet
nothing ever accepts a connection (immediate ECONNREFUSED, not a timeout,
so no firewall/NAT explanation fits) -- confirmed with a stock `ssh`
client on the same guest, localhost, so it is not the network path
either. The same binary, same flags, same user, launched from an
interactive shell or through one layer of `sh -c`, listens and accepts
connections correctly every time. Not yet root-caused inside
launch_daemon; documented here as the working shape rather than left for
the next person to rediscover.

Neither file ships just by existing under data/ -- build/jam/packages/Haiku
explicitly lists every boot script and launch file it packages (that is
how SetupEnvironment and data/launch/system/user get in at all), so this
also adds SshdKeygen to its bootScripts list and a matching
AddFilesToPackage block for data/launch/sshd.
diff --git a/build/jam/DefaultBuildProfiles b/build/jam/DefaultBuildProfiles
index 2999e2ae6b..4d0f6adb27 100644
--- a/build/jam/DefaultBuildProfiles
+++ b/build/jam/DefaultBuildProfiles
@@ -226,6 +226,20 @@ rule DefineDefaultBuildProfiles
 					webpositive
 					;
 			}
+
+			# OpenSSH: not on HaikuPorts for arm64 either (no port has been
+			# built for this architecture at all -- the real, non-bootstrap
+			# arm64 repository is empty). Cross-built against this tree's own
+			# openssl3/zlib using HaikuPorts' own net-misc/openssh patchset
+			# (10.4p1), minus libedit (not in the arm64 package set; it only
+			# gives sftp interactive line-editing). data/launch/sshd starts
+			# it at boot, after data/system/boot/SshdKeygen generates host
+			# keys on first run.
+			if $(TARGET_PACKAGING_ARCH) = arm64 {
+				AddHaikuImageSystemPackages
+					openssh
+					;
+			}
 		}
 
 		case "test-*" : {
diff --git a/build/jam/repositories/HaikuPorts/arm64 b/build/jam/repositories/HaikuPorts/arm64
index fecbe51d03..9b34d41ea3 100644
--- a/build/jam/repositories/HaikuPorts/arm64
+++ b/build/jam/repositories/HaikuPorts/arm64
@@ -71,6 +71,7 @@ RemotePackageRepository HaikuPorts
 	libavif1.0-1.1.1-1
 	sqlite3-3.50.4-1
 	webpositive-r1~beta6_hrev99000_dirty-1
+	openssh-10.4p1-1
 	:
 	# source packages
 	bash
diff --git a/data/launch/sshd b/data/launch/sshd
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..51e64376e7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/data/launch/sshd
@@ -0,0 +1,4 @@
+service x-vnd.Haiku-sshd {
+	launch /bin/sh -c "/bin/sh /system/boot/SshdKeygen; exec /system/sbin/sshd -D"
+	no_safemode
+}
diff --git a/data/system/boot/SshdKeygen b/data/system/boot/SshdKeygen
new file mode 100755
index 0000000000..3c90d3588c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/data/system/boot/SshdKeygen
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+#!/bin/sh
+# Materializes openssh's writable settings and generates host keys on first
+# boot. The openssh package ships only data/openssh/*.default -- packagefs
+# mounts the package itself read-only, so settings/ssh has to be populated
+# here rather than shipped directly in the package (see arm64-patch 0016).
+dir=/boot/system/settings/ssh
+mkdir -p "$dir"
+mkdir -p /boot/system/var/run
+[ -f "$dir/sshd_config" ] || cp /boot/system/data/openssh/sshd_config.default "$dir/sshd_config"
+[ -f "$dir/ssh_config" ] || cp /boot/system/data/openssh/ssh_config.default "$dir/ssh_config"
+[ -f "$dir/ssh_host_rsa_key" ] || /boot/system/bin/ssh-keygen -A >/dev/null 2>&1
+exit 0
diff --git a/build/jam/packages/Haiku b/build/jam/packages/Haiku
index 661c49cdf1..5a3825e9ce 100644
--- a/build/jam/packages/Haiku
+++ b/build/jam/packages/Haiku
@@ -253,7 +253,7 @@ AddSymlinkToPackage bin : trash : untrash ;
 AddSymlinkToPackage bin : less : more ;
 
 # scripts and data files
-local bootScripts = PostInstallScript SetupEnvironment ;
+local bootScripts = PostInstallScript SetupEnvironment SshdKeygen ;
 SEARCH on $(bootScripts) = [ FDirName $(HAIKU_TOP) data system boot ] ;
 AddFilesToPackage boot : $(bootScripts) ;
 
@@ -265,6 +265,10 @@ local userLaunchScripts = <data!launch>user ;
 SEARCH on $(userLaunchScripts) = [ FDirName $(HAIKU_TOP) data launch ] ;
 AddFilesToPackage data user_launch : $(userLaunchScripts) ;
 
+local sshdLaunchScript = <data!launch>sshd ;
+SEARCH on $(sshdLaunchScript) = [ FDirName $(HAIKU_TOP) data launch ] ;
+AddFilesToPackage data launch : $(sshdLaunchScript) ;
+
 # first login scripts
 local firstLoginFiles = default_deskbar_items.sh ;
 firstLoginFiles = $(firstLoginFiles:G=first-login) ;
